Z||000009||pHoOl||01-12-2001||04:51 PM||||With all due respect to anybody who has these flush mount headlights, i'm not sure that i see the purpose.  Other than doing your best to be different.  But to me it would be the same as if you did the same thing on a firebird.  With the bird, you'd end up with a pontiac camaro.  <P>just my $.02<P>------------------<BR>AIM: phool88fiero<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||01-12-2001||05:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pHoOl:<BR><B>With all due respect to anybody who has these flush mount headlights, i'm not sure that i see the purpose.  Other than doing your best to be different.  But to me it would be the same as if you did the same thing on a firebird.  With the bird, you'd end up with a pontiac camaro.  <P>just my $.02<P>I did a very similar setup on my Ferrari kit. I thought them sticking up was ugly myself, I never hardly used them-i used grill mounted driving lites instead. Now I can use my headlites without messing up the body lines, blink them to pass, and they never ever will stick again.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||DrRodey||01-12-2001||06:00 PM||||Found the link for the instructions...  <A HREF="http://fieroproject.com/tom/headlights.htm" TARGET=_blank>Toms Instuctions</A><BR>as for brightness, they are standard 55w headlights, the two outside ones are on for low beam all for are on for high beam.<P>pHoOl..Reasons for flush mount headlights<BR>1. headlights will never stick up or down again...<BR>2. no doors to flap at high speed<BR>3. headlight doors don't block your view of part of the road when up... cause they aren't<BR>4. some of us actually thing they look good.<BR>5. No one ever said we had to all be exactly the same. <BR>||||reg||1
